From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: b43: HT-PHY: take frames from the mac80211 TXQs when there is room

b43 left the TXQs to ieee80211_handle_wake_tx_queue(), which moves every
frame mac80211 has into one driver queue per AC as fast as it can, until
b43 stops the whole AC. Under load that queue held 100-270 frames (40-80 ms
at 50 Mbit/s), shared by all stations, and mac80211's per-station queueing
and fairness had nothing left to schedule:
- a phone in power save waited a median 46 ms after waking for frames
  that queued behind another station's traffic, often longer than it
  stayed awake (~95 ms), so pings to it took 0.4-1.5 s under load;
- with two stations downloading, the one with more queued data got most
  of the airtime.

Implement wake_tx_queue: the TX work takes frames only while a ring has
room for another A-MPDU and its driver queue is empty, one A-MPDU (or two
single frames) per ieee80211_next_txq() turn. A-MPDU frames without a
block ack, and frames held for a dozing station, go to a retry queue in
the txq's driver data, kept in sequence number order together with that
txq's frames still waiting in the driver queue, and are sent before newer
ones; the txq is scheduled again for them, and a dozing station's held
frames are reported with ieee80211_sta_set_buffered(). The frames in a
retry queue were dequeued, so AQL counts them as pending; once they exceed
the station's AQL limit, ieee80211_next_txq() skips the txq and they would
never be sent, so the TX work sends the retry queue of such a txq
directly. PS-Poll and uAPSD releases take the retry queue first, then
mac80211's queue. TX airtime is reported per PPDU with
ieee80211_sta_register_airtime(), and AIRTIME_FAIRNESS and AQL are
enabled. The module parameter ht_txq_pull=0 restores the old model.

On an R6400 AP with two clients: pings to a phone in power save under load
went from 460 ms average / 1.46 s maximum to 315-343 ms / 0.6-0.7 s, which
is what they take with no load at all; two UDP downloads get the same
airtime (9.2 s each in 20 s); the driver queue stays empty; single-client
throughput is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
